      "message": "Is there any documentation for the EC chip to confirm 1KB is the right page size? Although, I suppose the fact it builds and runs is likely good enough.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/third_party/zephyr/main/arch/arm/core/aarch32/cortex_m/Kconfig;rcl\u003d2904edc89bd720f94ee9c73524d798d3ca0da22c;l\u003d461\n\n```\nconfig CORTEX_M_NULL_POINTER_EXCEPTION_PAGE_SIZE\n\thex \"Size of paged unmapped to implement null pointer detection\"\n\tdefault 0x400\n\thelp\n\t  Size of the page reserved for detecting null pointer\n\t  dereferencing. Must be a power of two. A large value\n\t  offers enhanced detection performance to the cost of\n\t  wasting a large flash area that code may not use.\n```",
